From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Subject: [PATCH] service: keep the runtime directory across a restart

The warm-boot flag lives in the unit's RuntimeDirectory, which systemd
removes when the service stops. After a crash and Restart=on-failure the
daemon then finds no flag, starts in "Cold boot" mode and presets every
speaker model to cold, whatever the speakers' real temperature. Keep the
directory across restarts, as upstream speakersafetyd's unit does
(RuntimeDirectoryPreserve=restart).

Backport of the upstream unit line onto speakersafetyd 2.0.1.

--- a/speakersafetyd.service
+++ b/speakersafetyd.service
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 Type=simple
 ExecStart=/usr/bin/speakersafetyd -c /usr/share/speakersafetyd/ -m 7
 RuntimeDirectory=speakersafetyd
+RuntimeDirectoryPreserve=restart
 DynamicUser=true
 User=speakersafetyd
 Group=speakersafetyd
